{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Jack_of_All_Trades","to":"Jack of All Trades"},{"from":"Piercing_Wail","to":"Piercing Wail"},{"from":"Empty_Fist","to":"Empty Fist"},{"from":"Double_Tap","to":"Double Tap"},{"from":"Ghostly_Armor","to":"Ghostly Armor"},{"from":"Dodge_and_Roll","to":"Dodge and Roll"},{"from":"Riddle_with_Holes","to":"Riddle with Holes"},{"from":"Thinking_Ahead","to":"Thinking Ahead"}],"pages":{"2131":{"pageid":2131,"ns":0,"title":"Amplify","revisions":[{"revid":56167,"parentid":55622,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Rename|Amplify|Signal Boost}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Amplify\n|Image       = Blue-Amplify.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = This turn, your next (Power card is;2 Power cards are) played twice.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Amplify\n|Image        = Icon Amplify.png\n|Description  = Your next X {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} cards are played twice this turn.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Counter\n|BetweenTurns = Removed\n|Cap          = \n}}\n{{C|Amplify}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Amplify}}, which will make the following {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card(s) this turn play twice, for the first amount of cards equal to the amount of {{BD|Amplify}}. \n\nHaving more than 1 {{BD|Amplify}} will not increase the amount of times a single {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card is duplicated, but increases the amount of cards that can be duplicated when played.\n\nThe second play of these cards does not expend any {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The second play of a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card only starts after the first play is fully resolved. In effect, it is as if the two cards were played with a pause in between, resulting in interactions including but not limited to:\n** The first play of {{C|Heatsinks}} or {{C|Storm}} will already be activated by the second play.\n** The first play of {{C|After Image}} will already give {{KW|Block}} because of the second play.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The second play of a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card counts as the play of a wholly separate card. All consequences of playing that card will still apply:\n** The effects of the card itself.\n** Anything that triggers or increments upon playing a ({{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}}) card, including but not limited to: \n*** Effects such as {{BD|Storm}} or {{BD|Heatsink}}.\n*** Relics such as {{R|Bird-Faced Urn}} and {{R|Ink Bottle}}.\n*** Card limits such as {{R|Velvet Choker}} and the Time Eater's {{BD|Time Warp}}.  \n\n== Trivia ==\n* Along with {{C|Double Tap}} and {{C|Burst}}, one of the three 'play a card twice' Skills in the game.\n* In [[Slay the Spire 2:Main|Slay the Spire 2]], this card was redesigned into {{C2|Signal Boost}}.\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] shows the [[Defect]], [[Ironclad]], and [[Silent]] having a nice party. The [[Watcher]] was not invited.\n** She was not in the game at this time.\n** This card's [[Beta Art]] is likely a reference to the film ''Say Anything...''\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Loop'''\n** Updating icon for Amplify power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2269":{"pageid":2269,"ns":0,"title":"Crescendo","revisions":[{"revid":56951,"parentid":55712,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Crescendo\n|Image       = Purple-Crescendo.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}. <br>Enter {{KW|Wrath}}. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Wrath, Retain, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Wrath}}\n{{C|Crescendo}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It makes you enter the {{KW|Wrath}} {{KW|Stance}}. {{C|Crescendo}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As it {{KW|Retain|Retains}}, {{C|Establishment}} will decrease it in {{Icon|PE}}-cost at the end of a turn, unless it already costs 0. \n\n* When entering {{KW|Wrath}} if you are not in {{KW|Wrath}} yet:\n** If you have {{BD|Rushdown}} from {{C|Rushdown}}, you will draw that many cards.\n** You will switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n*** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n*** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n*** If you were in the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}} before, you will gain 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''', or 3 if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n* Being in {{KW|Wrath}} changes the effects of some cards:\n** {{C|Halt}} will give its additional {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{C|Indignation}} will apply {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* While in {{KW|Wrath}}, all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} damage you deal is doubled, but you also take double damage from enemy attacks.{{KW|Wrath}} only doubles damage from {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, not from effects such as {{BD|Panache}} or {{BD|Thorns}}, or relics such as {{R|Mercury Hourglass}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{KW|Wrath}} is worse than the {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}} in every way except for the aformentioned ones, using {{C|Crescendo}} while in {{KW|Divinity}} is generally bad.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2019":{"pageid":2019,"ns":0,"title":"Dodge and Roll","revisions":[{"revid":55744,"parentid":50481,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Dodge and Roll\n|Image       = Green-DodgeandRoll.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (4;6) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Next turn, gain (4;6) {{KW|Block}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Power Infobox|Next Turn Block}}\n{{C|Dodge and Roll}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 4 (6 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and 4 (6 if upgraded) {{BD|Next Turn Block}}, which will give that amount of {{KW|Block}} at the start of your next turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Next Turn Block}} is affected by {{BD|Dexterity}} and {{BD|Frail}} at the moment of gaining it, not at the moment of the {{KW|Block}} taking effect. This means that any {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|Frail}} you have at the moment of playing {{C|Dodge and Roll}} affects both the {{KW|Block}} you gain immediately and the {{KW|Block}} you gain next turn.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1910":{"pageid":1910,"ns":0,"title":"Double Tap","revisions":[{"revid":55747,"parentid":50458,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Rename|Double Tap|One-Two Punch}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Double Tap\n|Image       = Red-DoubleTap.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = This turn, your next (Attack is;2 Attacks are) played twice.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Double Tap}}\n{{C|Double Tap}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 1 (2 if upgraded) stacks of {{BD|Double Tap}}, which will make the following {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card(s) this turn play twice, for the first amount of cards equal to the amount of {{BD|Double Tap}}. \n\nHaving more than 1 {{BD|Double Tap}} will not increase the amount of times a single {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card is duplicated, but increases the amount of cards that can be duplicated when played.\n\nThe second play of these cards counts as a separate card being played, but this card is not added to your draw or discard pile, and is not {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} unless the card would {{KW|Exhaust}} upon being played normally. \n\nThe second play of these cards does not expend any {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy'''. The second play of an X-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card will use the same value of X as the first.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The second play of an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card only starts after the first play is fully resolved. In effect, it is as if the two cards were played with a pause in between, resulting in interactions including but not limited to:\n** The second play of {{C|Headbutt}} will be able to target the first play in the discard pile. \n** {{BD|Vigor}} will be consumed by the first play, and will not be used for the second play.\n** {{BD|Strength}} gained by {{R|Shuriken}} by the first play will already affect the second play.\n** {{BD|Malleable}} will already give the target {{KW|Block}} after the first play.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The second play of an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card counts as the play of a wholly separate card. All consequences of playing that card will still apply:\n** The effects of the card itself.\n** Anything that triggers or increments upon playing an ({{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}) card, including but not limited to: \n*** Effects such as {{BD|Rage}}.\n*** Relics such as {{R|Shuriken}} and {{R|Ink Bottle}}.\n*** Card limits such as {{R|Velvet Choker}} and the Time Eater's {{BD|Time Warp}}.  \n\n== Trivia ==\n\n* Along with {{C|Burst}} and {{C|Amplify}}, one of the three 'play a card twice' Skills in the game.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Fix for proper behavior when duplicating cards like Rampage and Genetic Algorithm with effects like Echo Form.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Double Tap power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Fixed issue where cards stayed after combat with Echo Form or Double Tap.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2278":{"pageid":2278,"ns":0,"title":"Empty Fist","revisions":[{"revid":54827,"parentid":50641,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Empty Fist\n|Image       = Purple-EmptyFist.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (9;14) damage.<br>Exit your {{KW|Stance}}.\n}}\n{{C|Empty Fist}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 9 (14 if upgraded) damage, and makes you exit your current {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{C|Empty Fist}} first deals damage and only then makes you exit your {{KW|Stance}}, meaning it can still benefit from the damage multiplication of {{KW|Wrath}} or {{KW|Divinity}} if you are in either {{KW|Stance}} when playing it.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* When you exit any {{KW|Stance}}, the following will occur:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n** When you exit {{KW|Calm}}, it has the additional effect of giving you 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''. This increases to 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2305":{"pageid":2305,"ns":0,"title":"Establishment","revisions":[{"revid":55765,"parentid":55424,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Establishment\n|Image       = Purple-Establishment.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = (;{{KW|Innate}}. )Whenever a card is {{KW|Retain|Retained}}, lower its cost by 1.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Establishment}}{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}}\n{{C|Establishment}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives one {{BD|Establishment}}, which lowers the {{Icon|PE}}-cost of all {{KW|Retain|Retained}} cards by one at the end of every turn they are {{KW|Retain|Retained}}. When upgraded, it becomes {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always appear in your first hand of combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Meditate}}, {{C|Well-Laid Plans}} and {{C|Equilibrium}} are cards that allow you to {{KW|Retain}} other cards and synergize well with {{C|Establishment}}, as they allows you to make any card cost 0 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' eventually.\n\n* Cards that have an {{Icon|PE}}-cost above 0 and {{KW|Retain}} on their own benefit from this card:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Flying Sleeves}}, {{C|Protect}}, {{C|Perseverance}} and {{C|Windmill Strike}}\n* {{C|Crescendo}} and {{C|Tranquility}}, although these already cost 0 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' when upgraded, meaning they then no longer benefit.\n* {{C|Sands of Time}} will decrease in {{Icon|PE}}-cost an additional time for every stack of {{BD|Establishment}}.\n* {{C|Worship}} and {{C|Blasphemy}}, only if upgraded.\n* {{C|Safety}} from {{C|Deceive Reality}}, and {{C|Smite}} from {{C|Battle Hymn}} or {{C|Carve Reality}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{R|Runic Pyramid}} does not {{KW|Retain}} cards, but prevents them from being [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]]. As a result of this, {{BD|Establishment}} does not reduce the cost of cards kept in hand through {{R|Runic Pyramid}} unless those cards are also under another actual {{KW|Retain}} effect.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1933":{"pageid":1933,"ns":0,"title":"Ghostly Armor","revisions":[{"revid":56759,"parentid":50430,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Ghostly Armor\n|Image       = Red-GhostlyArmor.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = {{KW|Ethereal}}.<br>Gain (10;13) {{KW|Block}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Ethereal, Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Ethereal}} {{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Ghostly Armor}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 10 (13 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}. It has {{KW|Ethereal}}, which means it will {{KW|Exhaust}} if it is in your hand when you end your turn.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** We removed one level of unlocks! Three additional cards are now available by default in the card pool for both The Silent and Ironclad. The following cards are now added to the card pool by default: Ghostly Armor, Carnage, Entrench\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1924":{"pageid":1924,"ns":0,"title":"Intimidate","revisions":[{"revid":56749,"parentid":55829,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Intimidate\n| Image       = Red-Intimidate.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Apply (1;2) {{BD|Weak}} to ALL enemies.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToEnemy = Weak\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Weak}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Intimidate}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It applies 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Weak}} to '''ALL''' enemies. {{C|Intimidate}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2458":{"pageid":2458,"ns":0,"title":"J.A.X.","revisions":[{"revid":55831,"parentid":50759,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = J.A.X.\n|Image       = Colorless-J.A.X..png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Lose 3 HP.<br>Gain (2;3) {{BD|Strength}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Strength}}\n{{C|J.A.X.}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It costs 3 HP to play, and gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Strength}}. \n\n== Obtaining J.A.X. ==\nCan only be obtained through the event {{E|Augmenter}} by choosing {{Frame|Test J.A.X.}}\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|J.A.X.}} can be used to trigger {{C|Rupture}}, {{R|Runic Cube}} and {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}, lower the cost of {{C|Blood for Blood}}, and control the activation of {{R|Centennial Puzzle}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The card's name is a play on words referring to \"getting jacked\", as in getting buff.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!'''\n** JAX card buffed. No longer exhausts.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** J.A.X. Dealer event's cost of J.A.X. updated 100 -> 77 Gold.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** J.A.X.+. 2 -> 3 Strength gain.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2468":{"pageid":2468,"ns":0,"title":"Jack of All Trades","revisions":[{"revid":50730,"parentid":36931,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Jack of All Trades\n|Image       = Colorless-JackofAllTrades.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Add (1;2) random Colorless (card;cards) into your hand.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Jack of All Trades}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It adds 1 (2 if upgraded) {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card(s) into your hand, after which this {{C|Jack of All Trades}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Obtaining Jack of All Trades ==\n{{C|Jack of All Trades}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a card generated by an upgraded {{C|Jack of All Trades}} exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n* Some {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat, or can only be obtained from another source. Below is a list of cards excluded from generation:\n** {{C|Bandage Up}}\n** {{C|Apparition}}\n** {{C|Bite}}\n** {{C|J.A.X.}}\n** {{C|Ritual Dagger}} \n** {{C|Shiv}}\n** {{C|Beta}}\n** {{C|Insight}}\n** {{C|Miracle}}\n** {{C|Omega}}\n** {{C|Safety}}\n** {{C|Smite}}\n** {{C|Through Violence}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 48: Creative AI'''\n** Capitalization fix: Jack Of All Trades -> Jack of All Trades.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like  Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 14: Bullet Time'''\n** Jack of All Trades has correct wording when upgraded.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Shiv and J.A.X can no longer spawn from effects like Jack Of All Trades and Transmutation.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Jack Of All Trades+. 1 random card -> 2 random cards.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2306":{"pageid":2306,"ns":0,"title":"Judgment","revisions":[{"revid":50702,"parentid":36433,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Judgment\n|Image       = Purple-Judgment.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = If the enemy has (30;40) or less HP, set their HP to 0.\n}}\n{{C|Judgment}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It deals no damage, but if the target has less than 30 (40 if upgraded) HP, it will set that enemy's HP to 0. In effect, depending on the current HP of the enemy, this either deals 30 (40) damage that bypasses {{KW|Block}}, or nothing.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]] [[Category:ToUpdate]]"}}}]},"2474":{"pageid":2474,"ns":0,"title":"Panacea","revisions":[{"revid":56637,"parentid":55884,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Panacea\n|Image       = Colorless-Panacea.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Gain (1;2) {{BD|Artifact}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Artifact, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Artifact}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Panacea}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Artifact}} and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Obtaining Panacea ==\n{{C|Panacea}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Its artwork may be a reference to an item with the same name from the game Dead Cells.\n* Prior to Patch 8, {{C|Panacea}} did not {{KW|Exhaust}} and had the following effect: Lose all {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Vulnerable}}, and {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Panacea reworked. Gain 1 Artifact. Exhaust. Upgrades to 2.\n\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Panacea card buffed to also remove Frail.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1823":{"pageid":1823,"ns":0,"title":"Piercing Wail","revisions":[{"revid":56377,"parentid":55896,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Piercing Wail\n| Image       = Green-PiercingWail.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = ALL enemies lose (6;8) {{BD|Strength}} this turn.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n| GivesToEnemy = Strength (Negative), Shackled\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Shackled}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Piercing Wail}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It applies '''negative''' 6 (8 if upgraded) {{BD|Strength}} to '''ALL''' enemies, and gives them the same amount of {{BD|Shackled}} to regain the missing {{BD|Strength}} at the end of their turn. {{C|Piercing Wail}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* The {{M|The Champ}}, the {{M|Awakened One}} and the {{M|Time Eater}} clear [[Debuffs]] when they are about to enter their second phase, meaning the {{BD|Strength}} penalty is maintained while {{BD|Shackled}} is removed. This means they get the {{BD|Strength}} penalty permanently instead of just that turn.\n** However, if this causes them to have '''negative''' {{BD|Strength}}, this will also be considered a [[Debuff]] and will be removed, leaving them with 0 {{BD|Strength}}.\n* The {{M|Corrupt Heart}} clears ''only'' '''negative''' {{BD|Strength}} when they buff (except for the turn 1 buff), meaning the {{BD|Strength}} penalty is removed but the {{BD|Shackled}} is maintained. This means it will permanently gain that amount of {{BD|Strength}} at the end of their turn.\n\n* {{C|Piercing Wail}} applies two effects per enemy: a [[Debuff]] to remove the {{BD|Strength}}, and {{BD|Shackled}} to add it back at end of turn. Despite this, enemies with {{BD|Artifact}} will still just lose one stack to negate the negative {{BD|Strength}}, without receiving the {{BD|Shackled}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] shows a {{M|Cultist}} going through the harrowing experience of listening to a screaming child.\n** Poor guy. (not the baby)\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 56: The Collector'''\n** Piercing Wail card is now 1.2s faster with Fast Mode.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 48: Creative AI'''\n** Certain enemies no longer gain extra strength when removing Piercing Wail or Dark Shackles from themselves.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating SFX for Piercing Wail.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Adding SFX for Piercing Wail card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 9: Ascension'''\n** Sadistic Nature no longer triggers twice from Shackles and Piercing Wail.\n\n* '''Weekle Patch 6: We're Back!'''\n** Enemies that remove debuffs no longer keep the str gain portion of Piercing Wail/Dark Shackles.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1826":{"pageid":1826,"ns":0,"title":"Rampage","revisions":[{"revid":55914,"parentid":50439,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Rampage\n|Image       = Red-Rampage.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal 8 damage.<br>Increase this card's damage by (5;8) this combat.\n}}\n{{C|Rampage}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 8 damage, and increases this damage by 5 (8 if upgraded) for the rest of combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* It synergizes with anything that allows it to be played sooner, such as {{C|Headbutt}}, {{P|Liquid Memories}} or {{C|Secret Weapon}}.\n** Decreasing the size of the deck through {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} cards can also increase the speed at which {{C|Rampage}} is played.\n\n* Playing it twice using an effect such as {{C|Double Tap}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}} will scale it twice as well, and the second play already has a damage increase from the first play.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Using {{C|Dual Wield}} or {{C|Nightmare}} for creating copies of {{C|Rampage}} during combat will copy the current damage, but afterwards these copies will scale differently.\n\n* Adding more copies of {{C|Rampage}} to the deck does not increase scaling speed, as each copy scales separately.\n\n* Only the actual damage is affected by {{BD|Strength}}, the damage with which the card scales is not.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Fix for proper behavior when duplicating cards like Rampage and Genetic Algorithm with effects like Echo Form.\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Rampage card's ramp increased from 4 -> 5. No change to upgraded version.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2257":{"pageid":2257,"ns":0,"title":"Recycle","revisions":[{"revid":53382,"parentid":50599,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation|0|1}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Recycle\n|Image       = Blue-Recycle.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = {{KW|Exhaust}} a card.<br>Gain {{Icon|BE}} equal to its cost.\n|Keywords    = Energy\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}} {{Keyword Infobox|Energy}} {{Sequel Rename|Recycle|Scavenge}}\n{{C|Recycle}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It allows you to pick a card in hand and {{KW|Exhaust}} it. If the card {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} had an {{Icon|BE}}-cost, gain that amount of {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* If the card is an X-cost card such as {{C|Reinforced Body}}, {{C|Tempest}}, or {{C|Multi-Cast}}, it will double your current {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2039":{"pageid":2039,"ns":0,"title":"Riddle with Holes","revisions":[{"revid":55923,"parentid":50520,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Riddle with Holes\n|Image       = Green-RiddlewithHoles.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal (3;4) damage 5 times.\n}}\n{{C|Riddle with Holes}} is a 2 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|The Boot}} significantly increases the damage output of this card. \n* Benefits 5 times from {{BD|Strength}} and {{BD|Vigor}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Title capitalization for Riddle With Holes -> Riddle with Holes.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2422":{"pageid":2422,"ns":0,"title":"Rushdown","revisions":[{"revid":55929,"parentid":55489,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Rushdown\n|Image       = Purple-Rushdown.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = Whenever you enter {{KW|Wrath}}, draw 2 cards.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Rushdown}} {{Keyword Infobox|Wrath}}\n{{C|Rushdown}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 2 {{BD|Rushdown}}, which makes you draw that amount of cards whenever you enter the {{KW|Wrath}} {{KW|Stance}}, as long as you were not in {{KW|Wrath}} before.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* If you enter {{KW|Wrath}} because of a card, that card will be placed into the discard pile, or draw pile in the case of {{C|Tantrum}}, before {{BD|Rushdown}} is triggered, meaning it is possible to immediately redraw that card.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Depends on being in {{KW|Wrath}}, meaning it synergizes with ways to enter that {{KW|Stance}}:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Eruption}}, {{C|Indignation}} and {{C|Tantrum}} can reliably make you enter {{KW|Wrath}}.\n* {{C|Crescendo}} can make you enter {{KW|Wrath}} once at any point after first drawing it, making it a good fallback.\n* {{C|Simmering Fury}} triggers after you draw the start of your turn, and gives extra draw on top of that, meaning this has a high chance of already filling your hand before {{BD|Rushdown}} can be useful.\n\n==== b) Potions ====\n* {{P|Stance Potion}} allows you to pick between entering {{KW|Calm}} and {{KW|Wrath}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* During beta testing Rushdown was called Adaptation, and triggered on all Stance changes. The internal name is still Adaptation.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2038":{"pageid":2038,"ns":0,"title":"Skewer","revisions":[{"revid":55942,"parentid":50522,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Skewer\n|Image       = Green-Skewer.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = -1\n|Description = Deal (7;10) damage X times.\n}}\n{{C|Skewer}} is an X {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (10 if upgraded) damage to X times.\n\nWhen playing an X {{Icon|GE}}-cost card, all {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' that you currently have will be consumed. The {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' consumed this way will be used as the value for X.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits X times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n* {{R|Chemical X}} makes {{C|Skewer}} hit 2 more times, regardless of the amount of {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' used to play it.\n* If {{C|Skewer}} is used with 2 or more {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''', it will be able to trigger {{R|Necronomicon}}.\n* If played using {{P|Distilled Chaos}}, {{C|Havoc}}, or {{C|Omniscience}}, it will play for the full current {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n* Can be used with 0 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' to advance {{R|Ink Bottle}}, {{R|Nunchaku}}, {{R|Kunai}}, {{R|Shuriken}}, and {{R|Ornamental Fan}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{C|Skewer}} is duplicated with an effect such as a {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Double Tap}}, the value of X will also be used for the copy.\n* Being an X-cost, {{C|Skewer}} can be targeted by {{C|Recycle}} to double the current {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy'''.\n* It will not count as a 0-cost card for {{R|Wrist Blade}}, {{C|All for One}} or {{C|Scrape}}, even with {{C|Swivel}}'s {{BD|Free Attack Power}} active.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The {{M|Red Louse}} is featured in the card art.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Removing 'Spend all [R].' from all X-cost cards for consistency.\n** Fixed bug where cost X cards do not work with energy gain cards if played too fast.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2479":{"pageid":2479,"ns":0,"title":"Thinking Ahead","revisions":[{"revid":50751,"parentid":36951,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Thinking Ahead\n|Image       = Colorless-ThinkingAhead.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Draw 2 cards.<br>Put a card from your hand on top of your draw pile.(<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.;)\n|Keywords    = Draw, Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Thinking Ahead}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 2 cards and allows you to select one card in hand to place on top of your drawpile. {{C|Thinking Ahead}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself, if it is not upgraded.\n\n== Obtaining Thinking Ahead ==\n{{C|Thinking Ahead}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Selecting the card to put on top of your draw pile happens ''after'' drawing, meaning a card drawn this way can potentially be placed right back on top.\n\n* Although {{C|Mayhem}} plays the top card of the draw pile, it cannot be used in tandem with {{C|Thinking Ahead}} to play a specific card, as {{C|Mayhem}} activates after cards are drawn at the start of your turn, meaning the card will already be in hand.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 19: Seed'''\n** Put vs Place wording inconsistency on Thinking Ahead and Exhume cards.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Thinking Ahead nerfed. Now exhausts. Upgrade removes Exhaust.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2431":{"pageid":2431,"ns":0,"title":"Void","revisions":[{"revid":53386,"parentid":50791,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Void\n|Image       = Colorless-Void.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Status\n|Rarity      = Status\n|Cost        = -2\n|NoUpgrade   = true\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>{{KW|Ethereal}}.<br>Whenever this card is drawn, lose 1 {{KW|Energy}}.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Energy\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}} {{Keyword Infobox|Ethereal}} {{Keyword Infobox|Energy}}\n{{C|Void}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|Common:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} Card. Whenever this card is drawn, lose 1 {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n== Obtaining Void ==\nPlaying {{C|TURBO}} will add a {{C|Void}} to the player's discard pile.\n\nThe following enemies can give the player {{C|Void}}:\n* {{M|Awakened One}}\n** {{Int|Awakened One|Sludge}} - Adds a {{C|Void}} into your draw pile.\n* {{M|Corrupt Heart}}\n** {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Debilitate}} - Adds 1 {{C|Void}} into your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Triggers the damage from {{C|Fire Breathing}}.\n* Draws cards with {{C|Evolve}}.\n* Is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{C|Second Wind}} and triggers its {{KW|Block}} gain.\n* Can be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} with {{R|Medical Kit}} to trigger exhaust synergies such as {{C|Feel No Pain}} or {{R|Charon's Ashes}}, or will {{KW|Exhaust}} on its own at the end of your turn.\n* Energy is only lost when the card is drawn. If the card is added to your hand by other means, such as with {{C|Seek}}, {{C|Hologram}}, or {{P|Liquid Memories}}, the energy reduction can be evaded.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{C|Sever Soul}} and {{C|Second Wind}}, since it is not an {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|Attack}} card.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Prevents {{C|Clash}} from being played.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 30: Skewer'''\n** Void card now resolves 0.25s faster.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Void card can no longer get you to negative energy.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face'''\n** Void: Replaces the Darkness debuff from the Awakened One.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}